From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:30:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] zones: The overlay spans the whole output, not the usable
 area.

The panel of layouts, the zones and the picker are drawn, and hit, in
the output's coordinates. With exclusive zone 0 the layout placed the
overlay in the usable area: On the output with the Clip, everything was
drawn shifted right by the Clip's width (64 px) from where the pointer
hits it. Dragging a window onto a layout or zone needed aiming left of
it; a click in the picker could snap to the neighbouring zone.
Exclusive zone -1: Not moved by other panels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/zones.c | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/zones.c b/src/zones.c
index 923f5ce..1a16584 100644
--- a/src/zones.c
+++ b/src/zones.c
@@ -759,11 +759,18 @@ static bool _wlmaker_zones_buffer_pointer_button(
     return true;
 }
 
-/** Overlay: Spans the whole output. */
+/**
+ * Overlay: Spans the whole output. The drawing and the pointer go by the
+ * output's box: With exclusive zone 0 the layout put the overlay in the
+ * usable area instead, ie. right of the Clip, and everything drawn was off
+ * by the Clip's width from where it is hit (the panel of layouts, the zones,
+ * the picker). -1: Not moved by other panels.
+ */
 static const wlmtk_panel_positioning_t _wlmaker_zones_positioning = {
     .desired_width = 0,
     .desired_height = 0,
-    .anchor = WLR_EDGE_BOTTOM | WLR_EDGE_TOP | WLR_EDGE_LEFT | WLR_EDGE_RIGHT
+    .anchor = WLR_EDGE_BOTTOM | WLR_EDGE_TOP | WLR_EDGE_LEFT | WLR_EDGE_RIGHT,
+    .exclusive_zone = -1
 };
 
 /** Panel's request_size: Remembers the size and redraws. */
